From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wshom: WScript.Network maps drives and connects printers

WScript.Network's drive and printer methods were E_NOTIMPL: logon scripts
(MapNetworkDrive, AddWindowsPrinterConnection, SetDefaultPrinter -- what
a domain's login script is made of) failed on the first call, and
EnumNetworkDrives and EnumPrinterConnections could not list anything.

- MapNetworkDrive and AddPrinterConnection make the connection
  (WNetAddConnection2, a disk or a printer port), with the user name and
  password when given, remembered when UpdateProfile is set;
  RemoveNetworkDrive and RemovePrinterConnection cancel it (Force,
  UpdateProfile), a \\server\printer connection with
  DeletePrinterConnection.
- EnumNetworkDrives and EnumPrinterConnections give the collection
  Windows does: local name, remote name, local name, ... (for printers,
  port and printer name).
- SetDefaultPrinter; AddWindowsPrinterConnection connects the printer (the
  driver and port arguments are for Windows 9x).
- The string collections are WshCollection objects (Item by position,
  Count, length, For Each).

Organization, Site and UserProfile stay E_NOTIMPL: Windows does not
implement them either.

Wine's wshom tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/wshnet-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit; two printers listed, the
default set, a share that is not there refused with a network error).
Mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_PRINTER_LIST (wshom.ocx/network.c).
